CORE
main.c
--32 --little-endian --unwind 5
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A copy of non-constant length into an int array used to leave the last
element unchanged when the copy ended at an element boundary (and so to change
nothing at all when it ended within the first element), and to fill a partly
copied last element from the wrong offset of the source when the copy did not
start at offset 0.
